# Tech stack (Web Admin — S2)

Reflects `package.json`. Changing this table requires an ADR under `docs/adr/`.

| Concern | Choice |
|---|---|
| Framework | **Next.js 16** App Router only — no Pages Router, no `getServerSideProps` |
| UI | React 19, function components + hooks. No class components |
| Language | TypeScript 5 strict. `any` banned — `unknown` + type guard, or a generic |
| Validation | **Zod 3** at the adapter boundary |
| Styling | **Tailwind CSS 4** + semantic CSS variables (`lib/theme/*`) |
| Unit tests | **Vitest 4** (`lib/**/*.test.ts`) |
| E2E | **Playwright** (`e2e/`, POM + fixtures) |

## Data access

- The web app calls the **Express API (S3) over HTTPS only**. It does not use
  the Supabase client, and it does not query Postgres — for reads or writes.
- Transport lives in `lib/api/*-adapter.ts` behind ports in `lib/ports/`.
  Bind at `lib/api/composition.ts` — the single composition root.
- Reads: Server Components call use-cases. Mutations: Server Actions →
  use-case → adapter → `revalidatePath` / `redirect`.
- Session: httpOnly cookie set after OTP/Google verify (ADR-0005). Never
  trust a lane, role, or `gym_org_id` sent from the client.

## Not installed — do not reach for these

`react-hook-form` · `@tanstack/react-query` · `swr` · `zustand` ·
`@supabase/supabase-js` · `clsx` / `tailwind-merge` (there is no `cn()` helper)

Forms use `useState` + `useTransition` + Server Actions. Server data is
fetched in RSCs, not client-side. Zustand is **documented but not installed**
(`state-management.mdc`) — install it only when a real shared-chrome slice
needs it, and say so first.

## Banned outright

- `any`
- Pages Router APIs
- default exports for components
- `fetch` of domain APIs inside client components — go through ports
- adapter imports outside `lib/api/composition.ts`
